{"id":"smith-wesson-model-686","slug":"smith-wesson-model-686","name":"Smith & Wesson Model 686","aliases":["SW 686","S&W686","S&W 686","S&W M686","Model 686","S&W Model 686","Smith Wesson 686","Smith & Wesson 686","Smith and wesson 686","Smith & Wesson Model 681"],"kind":"firearm","category":"revolvers","subcategory":"Revolver","description":"The Smith & Wesson Model 686 is a six- or seven-shot double-action revolver manufactured by Smith & Wesson and chambered for the .357 Magnum cartridge; it will also chamber and fire .38 Special cartridges. Smith & Wesson introduced the Model 686 in 1981. It is the stainless steel version of the Model 586, which features a blued steel finish. They are available ported and unported with a choice of 6- or 7-round cylinders.","development":"686 (no dash), 1981 Introduction model\n686-1, 1986 radius stud package, floating hand\n686-2, 1987 changed hammer nose, bushing and associated parts\n686-3, 1988 new yoke retention system\n686-4, 1993 change rear sight leaf, drill and tap frame, change extractor, Hogue grips\n686-5, 1997 change frame design to eliminate cylinder stop stud, eliminate serrated tangs, MIM hammer and trigger, change internal lock.\n686-6, 2001 internal lock\n686-7, 2003 Performance Center .38 Super, 6-Shot unfluted cylinder, 4\" barrel, Stainless Steel, 250 Made","facts":[],"specifications":[{"group":"Cartridge & Action","items":[{"label":"Cartridge","value":".357 Magnum, .38 Special"},{"label":"Action","value":"Double action and single action"},{"label":"Feed System","value":"6-round (686) or 7-round (686 Plus) cylinder"}]},{"group":"Dimensions","items":[{"label":"Weight","value":"1.25 kg","numeric":1.25,"unit":"kg"},{"label":"Length","value":"305 mm","numeric":305,"unit":"mm"},{"label":"Barrel Length","value":"2.5 in, 3 in, 4 in, 6 in, 8.325 in","numeric":2.5,"unit":"in"}]},{"group":"Production","items":[{"label":"Designed","value":"1980"},{"label":"Produced","value":"1981–present"}]},{"group":"Service","items":